: []}

**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** What a fit run records as its results (001 §L 'Results, stored in the fit run: value ± σ (Jacobian covariance; FitQuality REUSED); correlation matrix, rank, condition; per-experiment residuals and RMSE; Mueller realizability (coherency eigenvalues ≥ 0); the product check for series objects (M_comb against M_LR · M_QZ); post-fit identifiability by profile likelihood for suspect parameters'; step 383: 'S11.4 adds the results'). The shapes come first; steps 397-403 fill them and step 404 stores them in the fit run. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4, every case name has two words and no `bool` appears. In `FitRuns.fs` (step 383), after `ObjectMatrixFit` and before `FitRun`, in this order: (1) `FitEntryRef = { parameter : StudyParameterRef; owner : UnknownOwner }` (steps 358, 362), one entry of the fitted vector as `FitRunEntry` names it. (2) `FitCoordinate` = `EntryCoordinate of entries : FitEntryRef list` (the entries one coordinate of a solve is the value of: one in the nonlinear and object solves, every entry taking that stage-one constant in a calibration fit) | `ElementCoordinate of row : MuellerRowIndex * column : MuellerColumnIndex` (an element of a series' combined matrix, which no entry holds; `MuellerReconstruction.fs:MuellerRowIndex`, `:MuellerColumnIndex`) | `FringeVisibilityCoordinate` (the free visibility of the LP-LP AIR fringe, which stage one fits and no entry holds). (3) `FitProblemSubject` = `StudyEntriesProblem` (the nonlinear fit of the study residual and its priors) | `ObjectSolveProblem of items : ItemId list` (one linear object solve, a series' combined matrix when it names more than one item) | `AirFringeProblem of runs : ExperimentName list` (one stage-one AIR fringe fit of those runs). (4) Two `NumericCarrier`s, each a single-case union with `.value`: `JacobianColumnNorms of float[]` (a solve's Jacobian column norms, read whole from the `ResidualJacobian` carrier) and `CorrelationMatrix of float[][]` (a solve's parameter correlation matrix, read whole from the same carrier). (5) `FitProblemQuality = { subject : FitProblemSubject; coordinates : FitCoordinate list; rank : MatrixRank; conditionOpt : ConditionNumber option; columnNorms : JacobianColumnNorms; correlationOpt : CorrelationMatrix option; chiSquared : FitChiSquared; rmse : ResidualRmse }` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MatrixRank`, `:ResidualRmse`; `MuellerInverse.fs:ConditionNumber`): one solve's identifiability in its own coordinates (the nonlinear fit's scaled ones), the condition and the correlation present only where its Jacobian has full rank. (6) `FitEntrySigma = { entry : FitEntryRef; sigmaOpt : ParameterSigma option }` (step 214), one value's ± σ, `None` where its solve leaves it undetermined. (7) `RunResidual = { run : ExperimentName; residuals : ResidualVector; rmse : ResidualRmse }` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ResidualVector`), one fitted run's residual entries in the units of the solve that fitted it, and their root mean square. (8) `MuellerRealizability` = `RealizableMueller` | `UnrealizableMueller` (derived, never stored, so it carries no tag) and `ObjectRealizability = { item : ItemId; eigenvalues : CoherencyEigenvalue list }` (`MuellerInverse.fs:CoherencyEigenvalue`), one black-box object's four Cloude coherency eigenvalues at its fitted values, with `member this.realizability : MuellerRealizability`: `RealizableMueller` when every eigenvalue is at least −1.0e-12 times their sum (the coherency matrix's trace, its m₀₀), a round-off allowance on the positive semi-definite test `MuellerInverse.fs:cloudeEigenvalues` documents (a matrix is physically realizable if and only if no eigenvalue is negative), else `UnrealizableMueller`. (9) `SeriesProductCheck = { items : ItemId list; cascade : ParameterValue list; difference : MatrixDiff; fitRmse : ResidualRmse; productRmse : ResidualRmse }` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MatrixDiff`): a series' combined matrix against the cascade of its objects' own matrices, the cascade's sixteen elements row-major, step 352's readouts. (10) `SuspectReason` = `UndeterminedSigmaReason` (its solve leaves its σ undetermined) | `WideSigmaReason of fraction : SigmaFraction` (its σ over its bounds' span, past the threshold) | `CorrelatedEntryReason of partner : FitEntryRef * correlation : FitCorrelation` (its correlation with that entry, past the threshold) (step 395). (11) `ProfileOutcome` = `ProfileConverged of chiSquared : FitChiSquared` | `ProfileFailed of failure : FitMemberFailure` (step 383); `ProfilePoint = { value : ParameterValue; outcome : ProfileOutcome }`, one re-fit with the parameter held at `value`; and `ParameterProfile = { entry : FitEntryRef; reasons : SuspectReason list; points : ProfilePoint list }`, a suspect entry's χ² profile. (12) `FitRunResults = { sigmas : FitEntrySigma list; problems : FitProblemQuality list; runResiduals : RunResidual list; realizability : ObjectRealizability list; productChecks : SeriesProductCheck list; profiles : ParameterProfile list }`, a fit's results. The unions carrying payloads are stored in the serializer's case form, as `FitMemberOutcome` is (step 383); none carries a wire tag. No other type or member is added: the file form is step 404's. Tests, in `FitResultsTests`: `a fitted Mueller matrix is realizable when no coherency eigenvalue is negative beyond round-off`: an `ObjectRealizability` of `Propagation.identityMueller`'s `cloudeEigenvalues` and of `(MuellerReconstruction.retarderMueller (Angle.degree 30.0<deg>) (Retardance.degree 40.0<deg>)).cloudeEigenvalues` is `RealizableMueller`; of the diagonal Mueller matrix diag(1, 1.5, 0, 0), whose eigenvalues are 0.625, 0.625, −0.125 and −0.125, `UnrealizableMueller`; and of the literal eigenvalues 1, 0, 0 and −1e-14 `RealizableMueller`, of 1, 0, 0 and −1e-6 `UnrealizableMueller`.

**Acceptance.** After the shapes land, `FitRuns.fs` MUST declare the coordinate, subject, solve-quality, sigma, run-residual, realizability, product-check, suspect-reason and profile shapes and `FitRunResults`, and `ObjectRealizability.realizability` MUST flag a coherency eigenvalue negative beyond round-off; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a fitted Mueller matrix is realizable when no coherency eigenvalue is negative beyond round-off`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.
